# Refuse-case — after the feature lands, and it is the one file in this set that
# `check` ACCEPTS today (measured: exit 0, stdout `ok`).
#
# Claim: SPEC.md 1.3 gives `mut import: int = 1` as the example of a legal
# declaration in 0.1 and says "a program that uses them as names will need
# renaming the day one arrives".  This case is that day arriving: once `import`
# (and `from`/`as`) are claimed, this must stop being accepted.  If instead the
# design keeps them as contextual keywords that are only special at the start of
